    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: bezout-identity-oq-03-oq-04-oq-01\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nThis problem asks whether the direct CRT construction from `bezout-identity-oq-03-oq-04` can be generalized beyond `Z` to arbitrary commutative rings where Bezout identities are available. The target statement is a polymorphic CRT for coprime ideals `I_1, ..., I_n` in a Bezout ring `R`, identifying `R / (\\bigcap_i I_i)` with `\\prod_i R / I_i` via the canonical map.\n\n## Insights\n\nThe local notes identify Lean type class generalization as the main challenge, with `IsBezout`, `GCDMonoid`, and existing Mathlib Chinese remainder theorem support as the first APIs to investigate.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\nNo dead ends are recorded yet.\n"
